CORE broken-cprover-smt-backend no-new-smt
main.c
--arrays-uf-always
^\[main\.assertion\.9\] line \d+ assertion h->slots.*: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.10\] line \d+ assertion 0: FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^Invariant check failed
--
With --arrays-uf-always every array, also an array member of a struct that is
flattened (an element of an array of structs, a struct literal), is handled by
the array decision procedure where it is an operand of an equality.  Updates of
such members failed an invariant in convert_with_array, reads and equalities
failed invariants in arrayst, and the bits of an array symbol in a flattened
struct were not constrained to equal the array's elements.
